WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.500
Today we step into a college Russian kitchen to master everyday food words that will make your taste buds and your Russian skills happy.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:26.760
I am Olga, and this is привет, Русский, episode 70. Our word of the day is Malako, Malako. Break it down as Mo-Loko, with the stress on the last part. It means milk. Imagine a Mo-Loko cow doing a silly dance while giving you milk.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.500
Я пью молоко,

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.700
that means I drink milk,

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.080
repeat after me,

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.700
молоко, молоко.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.800
Now that you know молоко,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.420
let's add more kitchen words.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:38.940
Sir means cheese,

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:39.580
Sir,

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.000
repeat after me,

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:41.480
Sir,

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:42.060
Sir.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:43.760
Я ем Sir,

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.600
that means I eat cheese.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.540
Imagine Sir cheese sounds fancy,

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.100
just like a night's title.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:51.920
хлеб means bread,

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:52.620
хлеб,

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:53.700
repeat after me,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:54.800
хлеб, хлеб.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.320
хлеб вкусный,

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.220
Дотминс добрет из делиши.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.100
Синьков хлеб из дыхартибейс of every Russian meal.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.020
Яблоко means apple.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:04.840
Яблоко.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:05.880
Репит автами.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:06.740
Яблоко.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:07.480
Яблоко.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.260
Я люблю яблоко.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.080
Дотминс I love an apple.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.080
Яблоко sounds like yummy block, a tasty round fruit.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:16.720
Суп means soup.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:17.340
Суп.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.360
Репит автами.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:18.980
Суп.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.340
Суп.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:20.920
Горячий.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.620
Дотминс the soup is hot.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.880
Суп из супер вонит стимен on cold day.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.800
Мясо means meat, мясо, repeat after me, мясо, мясо.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.860
Мясо в супе, that means meat is in the soup.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.660
Мясо sounds like meaty or so good.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:41.080
Вода means water, вода, repeat after me, вода, вода.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.060
Я пью воду, that means I drink water.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.040
Вода is what you add to make tea or soup.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.100
Чай means tea, чай, repeat after me, чай, чай.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:55.740
Чай горячий, чай раймзвы с чай, да сам каузьи длинг.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:02.020
Вкусный минз делишас, вкусный, репет автами, вкусный, вкусный, вкусный, сыр вкусный,

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.540
вкусный taste like в укус, ям.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:10.120
Ремембер поездди from a few lessons ago, it means on the train, remember

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:14.140
большая, it means big, remember погода, it means weather.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.560
In Russian, the verb to eat changes depending on who is doing the action.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:25.920
Вы сей я ем, for I eat, for you eat, on or anna, yes, for he or she eats.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:29.960
This is different from English, where the verb stays almost the same.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:36.360
Now you can say, я ем сыр, that means I eat cheese, or ты ешь хлеб, that means

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.240
you eat bread.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:41.940
The word чай started in northern Chinese dialects, as ча.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.440
It traveled along the Silk Road through Central Asia.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.940
Это антердерашен в 17-м сентяне, как попелер-дринг-чай.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:51.460
Бей-керфол-доу.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:55.120
Рашен-ворт-чай-сounds exactly like the English-chai,

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.700
но это просто означает — same beverage, not a fancy latte.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.180
Пик-чай-стимин-кап-ов-чай, arriving by caravan from China,

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.100
straight to Russian Samovar.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:10.680
Дед-пик-чэх-хэп-с-де-ворт-стик. Рашен-слав-ширин-ти-эн-симпл-с-нэк-с-нэк-с,

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.300
like bread with cheese or soup when guests visit.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.420
Офирing food is a warm way to show hospitality and start a friendly conversation.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.300
It feels like opening your home with a steaming cup or bowl.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.940
Guests often feel instantly welcome around the table.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.040
Do you remember what Sir means?

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.140
Can you say the word for bread?

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.020
Try using the phrase «я-пю-малако» three times today.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:38.180
За кид с дрою фейфритрussian food like Sir or Yablaka,

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.140
и лабилит с раше ону.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:45.900
За адальс, next time you make tea or soup, say the Russian word out loud three times

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:46.700
while you cook.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.360
You did great today.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:52.040
Say today's words out loud one more time and they are yours.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:55.060
Share the show with a friend who wants to learn Russian,

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.880
and I'll see you next time.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:57.340
Пока.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:02.400
And if you'd rather watch, then listen, find us on YouTube at NERA-R-U.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.100
Links in the show notes.

